Remaining leaks seen while reading, NOT fixed: MooX::Cmd::Role does a bare use Carp; upstream, so croak is on every command class and karr cannot fix it from here (namespace::clean ruled out). Class-level (self-only) imports: Cmd/Backup, Cmd/Restore, Cmd/Init import Path::Tiny::path; Cmd/List, Cmd/Skill and others import user_error/clean_error; Pick/Move/Edit/Handoff/Context import Time::Piece. Those are classes, not roles, so each affects only itself.
Finding from the fix that corrects this ticket's own threat model, worth keeping for the #38 family: a Moo::Role-composed sub does NOT override a builtin for bare calls in the consumer -- probed directly, gmtime() inside a class composing ClaimTimeout still resolved to the builtin string. Only method calls ($cmd->gmtime) and fully-qualified calls ever saw the leak, and nothing in lib/ bin/ t/ calls either as a method. So the hazard was real but narrower than 'shadows builtins' suggests: it was a collision hazard, never a live miscomputation. The load-bearing half was the opposite direction -- (gmtime() - $claimed) in _claim_expired NEEDED Time::Piece's overloaded object, and reverting just that call to the builtin turns t/72 red in 2 of 4 subtests. A naive search-and-replace across both roles would have shipped a silent date bug.
